WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.313
What breaks, and what guards against it?

2
00:00:02.313 --> 00:00:06.244
A plan applied after it changed
would send a command nobody reviewed,

3
00:00:06.244 --> 00:00:09.349
so applying needs the approved
hash of the plan on disk.

4
00:00:09.349 --> 00:00:12.703
Lab evidence could start
production on fixture results,

5
00:00:12.703 --> 00:00:17.625
so fixture records never count, and the
production preflight checks the test stage.

6
00:00:17.625 --> 00:00:21.187
A standing write role would let
the reader change the estate,

7
00:00:21.187 --> 00:00:24.464
so reads need only Reader and
the plan's role is eligible

8
00:00:24.464 --> 00:00:27.813
through privileged identity
management, for the window.

9
00:00:27.813 --> 00:00:31.069
Output in a repository
would publish the register,

10
00:00:31.069 --> 00:00:35.412
so the preflight fails in the kit's
repository and warns in any other.

11
00:00:35.412 --> 00:00:40.455
And removal as production's rollback would
lose remediated resources and history,

12
00:00:40.455 --> 00:00:43.080
so production rolls back to audit instead.
